 category: **\"app\"**, **\"crash\"** (as \"crashes\"), **\"error\"**, **\"not working\"**, and **\"update\"**. No other categories exist in the supplied data. This is also the configured `default_category`.\n\n## Routing Decision\nRoute to **Technical Support** for diagnosis.\n\n## Policy Application\nThe frozen policy is: *\"Collect reproduction steps and device information, then route to technical support for diagnosis.\"*\n\n- The user has said that the crash started after an update and that an error appears.\n- The user has not given reproduction steps or device information. These must be collected before or alongside routing.\n\n## next_actions\n1. **Collect reproduction steps.** Ask what the user does just before the crash, and whether it happens at launch or on a specific screen.\n2. **Ask for device, browser or app version.** Ask for the device model, the OS and its version, and the app version installed after the update.\n3. **Route to Technical Support with logs if available.** Attach any crash logs, screenshots, or the exact error message.\n\n## Missing Information\nThe ticket does not include the following, so I have not assumed any of it:\n- The exact error message text or code\n- The device model and operating system (iOS or Android) with version\n- The app version and which update was installed\n- Reproduction steps, and whether the crash happens every time or only sometimes\n- Crash logs or screenshots\n- Whether a reinstall or cache clear has been tried\n\nI did not assign an incident severity, estimate how many users are affected, or name a known issue, because the provided data contains none of this.","ttft_ms":2140,"type":"result","duration_ms":7975,"uuid":"c8a74f89-3257-458a-8716-ab6692571436","ttft_stream_ms":1474,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1475,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
